RYDEX Privacy Policy
Last updated: July 4, 2026
1. Data We Collect
When you use RYDEX, we may collect and store:

Discord user IDs, usernames, and avatars
Server (guild) IDs and server configuration settings (automod rules, ticket categories, welcome/farewell messages, logging channels, etc.)
Message metadata needed for moderation features (e.g., invite/message counts for leaderboards)
Deleted/edited message content, held temporarily in memory only (for the snipe/edit-snipe commands), and automatically cleared on bot restart — never written to a database
Ticket transcripts, if your server uses the ticket system
Invite tracking data (who invited whom) for leaderboard features

2. How We Use Data
Collected data is used solely to provide RYDEX's features: moderation, automod, tickets, welcome/farewell messages, leaderboards, vanity roles, and related server management tools. We do not sell user data, and we do not use message content to train machine learning or AI models.
3. Data Storage
Data is stored in a managed PostgreSQL database (hosted via Supabase), which encrypts all data at rest using AES-256 and encrypts all connections via TLS. Data is retained for as long as RYDEX remains in your server or until deletion is requested.
4. Data Retention & Deletion
You can request deletion of your data (or your server's data) at any time by contacting us via our support server: https://discord.gg/xhQETNERVT. Upon request, we will remove the relevant records from our database.
5. Third Parties
RYDEX does not share your data with third parties except where required to operate a feature you've enabled (e.g., invite/leaderboard tracking uses Discord's own API).
6. Presence Data
RYDEX may read your online status and activity (Presence) to power commands like /status, /userinfo, and the Vanity Roles feature. Presence data is read live and is not stored.
7. Contact
For privacy questions or data requests, join our support server: https://discord.gg/eMSkYzfX9b
